    "problem": "User: Okay, so: A catalyst will provide a new path with a lower activation energy (Figure 1). Won't this mean the forward and backward reactions will both speed up (as they both have a lower activation energy path to take)? So then what's the point of using a catalyst? Or alternatively, how does the catalyst provide a net benefit for the forward reaction if both the forward and backward reaction\u2026",
